PRIVACY POLICY - Real Estate AI Analyzer (QLD)

Last Updated: [16/Mar/2026]

### Data Collection
REAhelper collects and processes the following user data:
- Real estate property listings and addresses
- Land valuation search queries
- Flood risk assessment queries
- User analysis results and preferences
- Browser history related to property searches (on realestate.com.au, qld.gov.au, fam.brisbane.qld.gov.au)

### Data Storage
- All data is stored **locally on your device** using Chrome's storage API
- No data is sent to external servers or third parties
- Analysis history is retained for 10 recent queries maximum
- All data persists only in your browser's local storage

### Permissions Usage
- **activeTab**: To access the currently viewed real estate property page
- **storage**: To save user preferences and analysis history locally
- **scripting**: To extract property data from web pages
- **sidePanel**: To display the analysis interface
- **Host Permissions** (realestate.com.au, qld.gov.au, fam.brisbane.qld.gov.au): To access property listings and government land/flood data

### Data Security
- Data is never transmitted over the network
- You can clear all stored data by clearing browser history/cache
- Manual delete options available in the extension for history and logs

### Third-Party Data
When you use the QLD Land Valuation or Brisbane FAM features, your searches are temporarily sent to those government websites. Please refer to their privacy policies:
- Queensland Government: https://www.qld.gov.au/
- Brisbane City Council: https://www.brisbane.qld.gov.au/

### User Control
Users can:
- Enable/disable land valuation lookups (setting: useLandValue)
- Enable/disable flood assessment lookups (setting: useBrisbaneFam)
- Clear analysis history at any time
- Clear browser cache to remove all stored data

